Tue Oct 27 10:57:06 UTC 2026 - Peter Simons <psimons@suse.com>

- Update dns to version 4.2.1.
  ## 4.2.1

  - Security: decoding a domain name could consume a lot of CPU time and
    memory with a crafted message (very long names or many compression
    pointers). Now names longer than 255 octets and names that follow
    more than 127 compression pointers are rejected.
  - Security: an undecodable UDP reply (possibly spoofed) aborted the
    lookup. Now it is dropped and the resolver keeps waiting.
  - The TTL of negative cache entries is now capped by `maximumTTL`.
  - Mailboxes are no longer stored in the domain name cache of the decoder.

